name: Recorded flows distinguish connected components and unreviewed roles
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_connectivity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: run threat-model:import {"path":"ctx.json","activate":true}
require-live-snap: 30 threat-model:import saved | imported
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 2 components have no recorded flows | map-review
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Map ✓ | accepted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_connectivity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART accepted
keys: G
require-live-snap: 25 Principal definition | unconnected-summary
expect: No incoming or outgoing flows recorded
expect-not: definition.Runtime
ask: Does Summary keep the recorded connected flows while identifying both components without recorded flows, without claiming that their roles are invalid or starting repair work?
keys: Enter z
require-live-snap: 25 No incoming or outgoing | selected-component-120x36
expect: Principal definition
resize: 160x48
live-snap: selected-component-160x48
expect: No incoming or outgoing
resize: 96x89
live-snap: selected-component-96x89
expect: No incoming or outgoing
resize: 80x24
live-snap: selected-component-80x24
expect: no recorded flows
resize: 60x20
live-snap: selected-component-60x20
expect: no recorded flows
expect: Resize to read selected details
resize: 40x12
live-snap: selected-component-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: selected-component-paged-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: selected-component-flow-notice-40x12
keys: NPage NPage NPage NPage
live-snap: selected-component-tail-40x12
keys: PPage
live-snap: selected-component-back-40x12
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_connectivity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART paged
ask: Is the selected component's missing recorded flow membership readable at all six sizes, with paging and existing context/scan controls preserved?
resize: 120x36
keys: k
require-live-snap: 25 Invoice definition | other-unconnected-component
keys: k
require-live-snap: 25 Owned records | connected-component
keys: j j
require-live-snap: 25 Principal definition | selected-component-restored
keys: s
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | separate-proposal
expect: No jobs started
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 25 Principal definition | proposal-return
expect: No incoming or outgoing
ask: Does changing selection show each component's own recorded flow membership, and does canceling a separate scan proposal preserve the original component without saving jobs or changing context?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_connectivity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART inspected
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME NO_COLOR=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 2 components have no recorded flows | restarted-summary
nav-mode:
keys: G Enter z
require-live-snap: 25 No incoming or outgoing | restarted-component
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/dfd_connectivity.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain the same context and source, both unconnected-component notices and unchanged zero job/request counts?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
